{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":397693},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":16639406}],"dockerImageVersionId":31401,"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":true}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/nihalcse/rlvs-dataset-preparation-and-splitting?scriptVersionId=329161289\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"id":"c78133621","cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n##  1: Project Overview \n\n# RLVS Dataset Preparation for Violence Detection\n\nThis notebook documents the complete dataset preparation pipeline used in the research project:\n\n1. RLVS Dataset Collection\n2. Frame Extraction\n3. Uniform Frame Sampling\n4. Dataset Splitting\n5. Final Dataset Structure\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"947dfe08-e1e5-4f14-8f06-676ef0045015","cell_type":"code","source":"##  2: Import Libraries\n\nimport os\nimport cv2\nimport random\nimport shutil\nimport numpy as np\n\nprint(\"Libraries Imported Successfully\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"50ccc424-a8c9-41d5-950f-ae456c40e95c","cell_type":"markdown","source":"##  3: RLVS Dataset Structure \n\n# Original RLVS Dataset Structure\n\nRLVS Dataset\n\n├── Violence\n│   ├── V_1.mp4\n│   ├── V_2.mp4\n│   └── ...\n│\n└── NonViolence\n├── NV_1.mp4\n├── NV_2.mp4\n└── ...","metadata":{}},{"id":"0dd04b79-19a4-4d1b-b225-fa9c80e7630b","cell_type":"code","source":"##  4: Frame Extraction\n\ndef extract_frames(video_path, output_folder):\n\n```\nos.makedirs(output_folder, exist_ok=True)\n\ncap = cv2.VideoCapture(video_path)\n\ncount = 0\n\nwhile True:\n\n    success, frame = cap.read()\n\n    if not success:\n        break\n\n    frame_path = os.path.join(\n        output_folder,\n        f\"frame_{count:04d}.jpg\"\n    )\n\n    cv2.imwrite(frame_path, frame)\n\n    count += 1\n\ncap.release()\n\nprint(f\"Extracted {count} frames\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"a83a7d97-07af-43e3-b327-ed177b7531df","cell_type":"code","source":"##  5: Uniform Sampling\n\ndef uniform_sampling(frame_list, sequence_length=20):\n\n```\ntotal = len(frame_list)\n\nif total >= sequence_length:\n\n    indices = np.linspace(\n        0,\n        total - 1,\n        sequence_length\n    ).astype(int)\n\n    sampled_frames = [\n        frame_list[i]\n        for i in indices\n    ]\n\nelse:\n\n    sampled_frames = frame_list.copy()\n\n    while len(sampled_frames) < sequence_length:\n        sampled_frames.append(\n            sampled_frames[-1]\n        )\n\nreturn sampled_frames","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"3bee2174-e567-4f0f-bedd-6ffc001b93d7","cell_type":"markdown","source":"##  6: Explanation \n\n# Uniform Frame Sampling\n\nThe model expects exactly 20 frames from every video.\n\nIf a video contains more than 20 frames:\n\n* Select 20 equally spaced frames.\n\nIf a video contains fewer than 20 frames:\n\n* Repeat the last frame until 20 frames are available.\n\nThis ensures a fixed-length temporal sequence for the BiLSTM.","metadata":{}},{"id":"bb28cadc-efec-4e77-b2a6-ab3e91b967e8","cell_type":"code","source":"##  7: Dataset Splitting\n\nrandom.seed(42)\n\nTRAIN_RATIO = 0.70\nVAL_RATIO = 0.15\nTEST_RATIO = 0.15\n\nSOURCE_DIR = \"dataset_frames\"\n\nfor cls in [\"violence\", \"nonviolence\"]:\n\n```\nclass_path = os.path.join(\n    SOURCE_DIR,\n    cls\n)\n\nvideos = os.listdir(class_path)\n\nrandom.shuffle(videos)\n\nn = len(videos)\n\ntrain_end = int(n * TRAIN_RATIO)\nval_end = int(n * (TRAIN_RATIO + VAL_RATIO))\n\ntrain_videos = videos[:train_end]\nval_videos = videos[train_end:val_end]\ntest_videos = videos[val_end:]\n\nprint(f\"\\nClass: {cls}\")\nprint(\"Train:\", len(train_videos))\nprint(\"Validation:\", len(val_videos))\nprint(\"Test:\", len(test_videos))","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"e3c66b98-9274-41b1-b55c-4c9608401645","cell_type":"markdown","source":"##  8: Final Dataset Structure \n\n# Final Dataset Structure\n\ndataset_frames\n\n├── train\n│   ├── violence\n│   └── nonviolence\n│\n├── val\n│   ├── violence\n│   └── nonviolence\n│\n└── test\n├── violence\n└── nonviolence","metadata":{}},{"id":"927ff702-fc31-4f49-9683-ffd8f70d27a7","cell_type":"code","source":"##  9: Dataset Statistics\n\nbase_path = \"dataset_frames\"\n\nfor split in [\"train\", \"val\", \"test\"]:\n\n```\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*40)\nprint(split.upper())\nprint(\"=\"*40)\n\nfor cls in [\"violence\", \"nonviolence\"]:\n\n    path = os.path.join(\n        base_path,\n        split,\n        cls\n    )\n\n    if os.path.exists(path):\n\n        count = len(os.listdir(path))\n\n        print(\n            f\"{cls}: {count}\"\n        )","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"b226a658-8656-4ff2-8083-70414b3bbda6","cell_type":"markdown","source":"##  10: Research Methodology \n\n# Dataset Preparation Methodology\n\nThe Real-Life Violence Situations (RLVS) dataset was used as the source dataset.\n\nVideo samples were converted into image frames using OpenCV-based frame extraction.\n\nTo ensure consistent temporal input for the ResNet18-BiLSTM model, uniform frame sampling was applied. Twenty representative frames were selected from each video sequence.\n\nThe processed samples were divided into training, validation, and testing subsets using a fixed random seed (42) to ensure reproducibility.\n\nThe final dataset structure consisted of train, validation, and test folders, each containing violence and non-violence classes.\n\nThis prepared dataset was subsequently used for model training, hyperparameter tuning, and final performance evaluation.","metadata":{}}]}